  "body": "**Main is red:** `crates/app/tests/coarse_laws.rs` fails 4 tests on upstream main.\n\n**Cause:** two merged PRs interacted. PR #1064 (#904, merged 2026-11-12 09:05Z) added `coarse_laws.rs`, whose expected refusal (line 124) reads \"re-import with a larger budget\". PR #1074 (#1054, merged 10:34Z) reworded `model_fidelity::TOO_COARSE` to \"re-import with a larger STEP facet budget\" and updated the suites it knew (`model_fidelity.rs`, `step_budget.rs`), but not `coarse_laws.rs`, which didn't exist on its branch. Each PR was green alone.\n\n**Evidence:** found by the #1093 worker (PR #1177, a golden-only change on upstream/main 6a10c5ad): exactly these 4 `coarse_laws` tests fail on a message mismatch, and nothing else does. On main, `coarse_laws.rs:124` formats \"...re-import with a larger budget (surfaces are approximated to within {mm} mm)\" against `model_fidelity.rs:42`'s \"...re-import with a larger STEP facet budget\".\n\n**Done means:** `coarse_laws.rs` expects the current wording (test-only fix, no behaviour change), and the suite is green on main.\n",
